    <item>
      <title>v1.5.8 — Dark/Light theme switch</title>
      <link>https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/speedtab/adkjbdepojalajhfkoobiedddlnoamff</link>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">speedtab-news-158</guid>
      <pubDate>Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:00:00 GMT</pubDate>
      <dc:creator>Speedy E</dc:creator>
      <description><![CDATA[
        <p data-st-text-align="center" data-st-margin-bottom="16px" data-st-margin-top="0">
          <b>Try it right now</b> — this switch controls Speedtab's theme in real time:
        </p>

        <div data-st-display="flex"
            data-st-justify-content="center"
            data-st-margin-bottom="16px">
          <label data-switch-component class="reverse-component-grid">
            <input type="checkbox"
                  role="switch"
                  aria-label="Toggle shell theme"
                  data-change="stToggleColorPreset"
                  data-state-sync="shell-theme"
                  value="light"
                  data-toggle-value="dark">
            <span class="state" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="container"><span class="knob"></span></span>
              <span class="off">Dark</span>
              <span class="on">Light</span>
            </span>
          </label>
        </div>

        <p data-st-margin="0"
          data-st-text-align="center"
          data-st-font-size="0.85rem"
          data-st-opacity="0.75">
          Yes — that's a real, working control inside a feed item.
          Same pattern as YaiTabs: <code>data-change</code> + YEH delegation.
        </p>
      ]]></description>
    </item>

